# Orca — agent routing (Cursor vs Codex)

When spawning Orca workers (`worker-start --agent …`), pick the agent by **task kind**:

| Task kind | `--agent` | Notes |
| --------- | --------- | ----- |
| Implementation / coding / fix / migrate / tests that write code | `cursor` | Default for all ownership slices (BE / web / iOS / coordinator code) |
| Plan, design, spike write-up, architecture choice, design critique | `codex` | Prefer Codex; do not use Codex as the primary coding worker |
| Plan/design when Codex unavailable | `cursor` | Fallback only |
| DoD / acceptance review of implementation (Issue → Chờ duyệt) | `cursor` | Always spawn one Cursor reviewer ≠ implementer; no user approval gate — see `github-project-tracking.mdc` |
| Security-sensitive review (RLS/authz/races) | `cursor` | Independent of implementer; may be separate from DoD; both require exact-SHA evidence |

## DoD / security review — bắt buộc trong spec

Spec reviewer phải gồm:

1. Issue # / PR # / paths  
2. **Exact commit SHA(s)** đang duyệt (`git rev-parse`)  
3. Checklist DoD hoặc security  
4. Yêu cầu báo cáo: reviewer/session id hoặc worktree, checks đã chạy, findings/limitations, verdict PASS|FAIL|PASS with known gap  
5. Nếu SHA đổi hành vi sau review trước → revalidation; cấm tái dùng verdict  

**Thiếu GitHub PR review UI ≠ thiếu Orca review.** Reviewer ghi artifact (Issue/PR comment hoặc `docs/reviews/*`) với SHA; coordinator không được đánh FAIL chỉ vì GitHub “Reviewers: none” khi artifact Orca Cursor DoD hợp lệ đã có.

## Fallback (Codex quota / launch failure)

If `worker-start --agent codex` fails (quota, auth, launch error) or the worker reports quota exhaustion:

1. Retry the **same Task** with `--agent cursor` (same `--spec` / `--task`, same scope).
2. Note in the coordinator report: Codex unavailable → Cursor fallback for plan/review.
3. Do **not** switch coding workers from Cursor to Codex to “save” Cursor quota.

## Examples

```text
✅ Coding (parallel wave):
ORCA orchestration worker-start --spec "<BE impl>" --worktree current --agent cursor --json
ORCA orchestration worker-start --spec "<web impl>" --worktree current --agent cursor --json

✅ Plan (Codex) then DoD review (Cursor) with exact SHA:
ORCA orchestration worker-start --spec "<plan D1 membership>" --worktree current --agent codex --json
ORCA orchestration worker-start --spec "<DoD review Issue #N PR #M SHA abc123…; paths; checklist>" --worktree current --agent cursor --json

✅ Codex quota exhausted on plan → retry plan with --agent cursor

✅ Queue full → prioritize Cursor DoD/security workers over new feature coding (see idle-fill + parallel rules)

❌ Coding worker with --agent codex
❌ Skip Cursor DoD reviewer and mark Project Hoàn thành
❌ DoD pass without naming exact SHA / without independent session
❌ Plan/DoD review with --agent claude (or other) unless the user names that agent
❌ Treat “no GitHub approve” as proof that Orca DoD never ran
```

## Overrides

- User explicitly names an agent/model → honor that for that Task.
- Still respect ownership scopes, parallel-first coding, and WIP backpressure (see `orca-parallel-workers.mdc`, `orca-idle-worker-fill.mdc`).
